<title>HONG KONG: Int'l investors eye Asian credits at HK roadshow.</title>
<headline>Int'l investors eye Asian credits at HK roadshow.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>International investors, increasingly keen to add Asian debt instruments to their portfolios, will be meeting with Asian issuers in a seven-city roadshow beginning Monday in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>The roadshow, sponsored by U.S. investment bank J.P. Morgan, groups key Asian borrowers with 25 investors from the United States as well as 40 Asian and European investors.</p>
<p>Asian issuers are becoming increasingly sophisticated in their borrowing and some of the higher-rated names are frequent issuers in the Eurobond and Yankee markets.</p>
<p>Issuers making presentations in Hong Kong include the Ministry of Finance of China, Malaysia's Tenaga Nasional Berhad, Hong Kong's China Light and Power and Mass Transit Railway Corp and South Korea quasi-sovereigns Korea Development Bank and Korea Electric Power Co.</p>
<p>J.P. Morgan said the investors will visit Manila, Jakarta, Bangkok, New Delhi and Bombay later this week.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371</p>
</text>
